Cell["Prelude to storing and retrieving: why SolutionsX?", "Section",
 CellID->1748,ExpressionUUID->"c1b15b43-efde-4577-b8fb-625a16abee4d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "So far, nothing in this notebook strictly requires SolutionsX \[LongDash] \
the entire environment can be made using xAct alone. A key feature that \
SolutionsX introduces is that during the entire build-up the user is forced \
to be populating the association sol as they introduce all the xAct entities \
and as they do computations on them. sol now acts as a set of instructions on \
how to re-build the current xAct environment from scratch. The utility of \
this is clear from the above example: a lot of work goes into creating the \
xAct environment for the 5d STU model. From now on, towards describing any \
solution of that theory, one simply calls the pre-existing environment and \
starts building on top of it. Applying the function ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["SaveData"]], "paclet:VasilDimitrov/SolutionsX/ref/SaveData", 
    "VasilDimitrov Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
